HST Office: File panel pages other than Home are laid out when they are shown.

The File panel (hst-file-dropdown.patch) is a weld::Popover. On Windows, macOS and gen it is a
floating popup window (SalInstancePopover) whose content is laid out when it pops up, on its Home
page. ShowPage only switches the visibility of the page boxes, and a page shown while the panel is
open got no allocation: New, Open, Info and Save As stayed blank, Home showed again. Reported on
test PC HST4 (Windows 11, trial of main 24696ac: Info empty, no USB Token or "Phiên bản trước"
button) and reproduced with the Linux build of 24696ac under the gen plugin: every page but Home
blank, also with the "Phiên bản trước" button hidden or the Info page visible from the start, so
neither that button nor the profile is the cause.

ShowPage lays the open panel out again (resize_to_request) after switching pages. GTK lays out its
own popover and is left alone.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
Test: gen under Xvfb (SAL_USE_VCLPLUGIN=gen), File panel ▸ Mới, Mở, Thông tin, Lưu thành show
their content; Windows the same; GTK unchanged.
---
--- a/sfx2/source/backstage/hstbackstagewindow.cxx
+++ b/sfx2/source/backstage/hstbackstagewindow.cxx
@@ -639,6 +639,12 @@
         FillInfoPage();
     else if (ePage == Page::SaveAs)
         FillSaveAsPage();
+
+    // The floating popup of the other plugins (SalInstancePopover: Windows, macOS, gen) lays its
+    // content out only when it pops up, so a page shown afterwards kept no size and stayed blank
+    // (every page but Home, the page of the popup): lay the panel out again for the new page.
+    if (m_bOpen && m_xPopover->get_visible() && !Application::GetToolkitName().startsWith("gtk"))
+        m_xPopover->resize_to_request();
 }
 
 void BackstageWindow::FillRecentLists()
